From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:00:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/37] tools/aurora-sep: CPU PD always saves about 1 W; add
 wakelat.c and an opt-in rule

30 paired rounds on a busy M2 Pro: disabling WFI, so every idle entry is
CPU PD, used 0.99 W less (standard error 0.20 W) than the menu governor's
choices, which with the 10 ms target residency almost never pick CPU PD.
wakelat.c measured the cost: about 10 us added to each wake-up, as the
state declares. cpuidle-pd-always.tmpfiles.conf makes the setting
persistent for those who want it now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AuzUDcEeRJQ6RCdWW2XWLb
